5. Visualizing the "Algorithm" (The Trust Factor)
Since the company is the "Security Guard," you should add a "Risk Shield" visual to the cards. This explains why the group is safe without needing a "tough" Admin.

UX Elements for the "Company Protection"
The "Live Monitor" Icon: A small pulsing green dot on the card that says: "Algorithm actively monitoring group liquidity."

The "Safety Net" Tag:
    A tag that says: "100% Principal Protected by [Company Name]."

Summary of the Shift
Old Way: Admin = The Enforcer (gets a cut, risks friendships).

Your Way: Admin = The Host (gets platform perks, builds social status).

The Company: The Invisible Enforcer (takes the risk, earns the trust).


